  "slug": "reveals-genome-9303",
  "summary": "Two draft marine genomes and two updated clade databases add reference and multi-omics resources for tubeworms, red algae, planarians and stony corals.",
  "synthesis": "The items share a focus on genomic resources for non-model eukaryotes, mostly marine. Two preprints report de novo assemblies. The seep tubeworm Lamellibrachia satsuma draft (665 Mb, 6,320 scaffolds) combines Nanopore and Illumina data with annotation. The red seaweed Furcellaria lumbricalis reference comes from a species occurring across a broad salinity gradient, from the saline NE Atlantic to the brackish Baltic. Two database papers work at clade level. PlanMine 4.0 adds new planarian genomes, 70 flatworm transcriptomes and expression resources. CoralDB provides a functional and evolutionary multi-omics resource for stony corals. The new elements are the added taxa and the integration of genomes, transcriptomes and expression data. The summaries do not report downstream comparative analyses.",
